30bp in Q3 to 165bp.\n- Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond \"comfortably\". Its 2027 capex is planned up 12%, so it can probably fund most of that with debt.\n- Pellham Power is the largest buyer of grid equipment in Caldria. I found no sign it plans to replace its failed equity raise with bonds. The sources don't say why. Leverage limits, ratings limits or the wider spreads are possible reasons.\n\n**Equity markets (mostly no)**\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size, so the weakness isn't only Pellham's.\n- The \"mostly no\" rests on one withdrawn deal and two downsized ones. I couldn't check whether stronger utilities such as Norvane could still raise equity, or at what discount.\n\n**Implication**\n- Pellham had planned 2027 capex up 18%. It now says it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes \"until financing improves\".\n- Expect healthy issuers to lean on debt and some capex to slip. The slippage hits grid-equipment demand directly.\n\n**Gaps**\n- I found no data on issuer leverage, ratings, or the total debt needed.\n\nChild results are in n5.r1 (debt) and n6.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":3502,"type":"result","duration_ms":30858,"uuid":"bfb621b1-33a5-4dc4-b78c-de339f290825","ttft_stream_ms":3218,"time_to_request_ms":136,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":10,"system_prompt":13,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":33,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":19,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":13,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":4,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":23,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":79,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"